    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "Customer churn is a major challenge in the telecommunications industry, where customers may discontinue services due to various reasons such as high costs, poor service quality, or better alternatives. Predicting customer churn helps companies identify at-risk customers in advance and take actions to retain them.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this project, machine learning classification techniques are applied to analyze customer data and predict whether a customer is likely to churn or not. The project evaluates models **before and after preprocessing** to demonstrate the impact of data preparation on model performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Objective |\n",
    "|---|-----------|\n",
    "| 1 | Build and evaluate multiple classification models on the IBM Telco dataset |\n",
    "| 2 | Compare model performance before and after data preprocessing |\n",
    "| 3 | Identify the most effective model using Recall and F1 Score |\n",
    "| 4 | Derive business insights to improve customer retention |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Pipeline Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "| Step | Task |\n",
    "|------|------|\n",
    "| 0 | Install required libraries |\n",
    "| 1 | Import libraries |\n",
    "| 2 | Load, clean & inspect dataset |\n",
    "| 3 | Minimal preprocessing (Raw pipeline) |\n",
    "| 4 | Train models on raw data (DT, Rule-Based, LR, KNN) |\n",
    "| 5 | Full preprocessing (SMOTE + Scaling) |\n",
    "| 6 | Train models on preprocessed data |\n",
    "| 7 | Final comparison across all models |"
   ]
  },
