    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Step 3: Minimal Preprocessing - Raw Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "Raw data is minimally preprocessed to make it compatible with scikit-learn.  \n",
    "Only encoding and basic cleaning are applied. Advanced techniques (SMOTE, scaling) are applied later.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dropped Columns\n",
    "\n",
    "| Column | Reason |\n",
    "|--------|--------|\n",
    "| `CustomerID`, `Count` | Unique identifiers - no predictive value |\n",
    "| `Country`, `State`, `City`, `Zip Code`, `Lat Long`, `Latitude`, `Longitude` | Too noisy, geographically granular |\n",
    "| `Churn Reason` | **Data leakage** - post-outcome information |\n",
    "| `Churn Label`, `Churn Score`, `CLTV` | Derived from churn outcome - leakage |\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Data Leakage:** Occurs when a column contains future/post-outcome information, causing artificially high accuracy that does not generalise to real-world use."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "a8e6041b3f1c64a5",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-05-20T20:47:12.583563Z",
     "start_time": "2026-05-20T20:47:12.542803Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Raw Pipeline Summary\n",
      "====================================================\n",
      "  Columns after drop      : 20\n",
      "  Missing values imputed  : 11 (Total Charges)\n",
      "  Columns label-encoded   : 16\n",
      "  Final shape             : (7043, 20)\n",
      "====================================================\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df_raw = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "LEAKAGE_COLS = [\n",
    "    'CustomerID', 'Count', 'Country', 'State', 'City',\n",
    "    'Zip Code', 'Lat Long', 'Latitude', 'Longitude',\n",
    "    'Churn Reason', 'Churn Label', 'Churn Score', 'CLTV'\n",
    "]\n",
    "df_raw.drop(LEAKAGE_COLS, axis=1, inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert Total Charges to numeric\n",
    "df_raw['Total Charges'] = pd.to_numeric(df_raw['Total Charges'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Impute missing values with median (robust to outliers)\n",
    "missing_before = df_raw['Total Charges'].isnull().sum()\n",
    "df_raw['Total Charges'].fillna(df_raw['Total Charges'].median(), inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Label-encode all categorical columns\n",
    "le = LabelEncoder()\n",
    "encoded_cols = []\n",
    "for col in df_raw.columns:\n",
    "    if df_raw[col].dtype == 'object':\n",
    "        df_raw[col] = le.fit_transform(df_raw[col])\n",
    "        encoded_cols.append(col)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Raw Pipeline Summary')\n",
    "print('=' * 52)\n",
    "print(f'  Columns after drop      : {df_raw.shape[1]}')\n",
    "print(f'  Missing values imputed  : {missing_before} (Total Charges)')\n",
    "print(f'  Columns label-encoded   : {len(encoded_cols)}')\n",
    "print(f'  Final shape             : {df_raw.shape}')\n",
    "print('=' * 52)"
   ]
  },
